# Modules nest to any depth (claude/modules-style-pass.md, Jimmy's ruling of 5 November):
# every `mod Name` declares a child module named by its dotted path, whose file is
# `name.prism` beside the declaring file, or `name/mod.prism` when it has children of its
# own. Here `Shapes.Round.Circle` is a file at depth 3 and `Shapes.Round.Oval` a directory
# at depth 3 with the file `Shapes.Round.Oval.Egg` under it; siblings and parents use each
# other by full path, both ways. `Shapes.Static` and `Shapes.Switch` are named by a Rust
# and a C++ keyword: each target escapes the module's name as it escapes any other.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Shapes
test mod Tests
use Ui
use Shapes.Round.Circle.*

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Area 2} {Shapes.Flat.Area 3} {Shapes.Total 1}")
